From eeb086412805f4eb20d70248ea3e10b6606fc942 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bench <bench@local>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:56:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] null patch: 60-per-entity-systems-where-read

update_fluid_on_eyes runs only for the bot's own entity and update_in_loaded_chunk only for entities marked ReadsInLoadedChunk (nothing in the fork sets it). With one World per bot each bot holds a copy of every other bot, and these two systems were about 40 percent of the CPU that own worlds add. Every reader (mining, auto tool, loading, events) sits on the bot's own entity. Null-only: a user query of InLoadedChunk on mobs no longer finds the flag.

Vanilla: Entity#updateFluidOnEyes runs for every entity, but no client decision reads another entity's value. Grim: no packet depends on a copy's value.
